    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "CITYWIDE present Apt 21, Pier 19, a stylishly presented 1st floor 2 bedroom apartment, with a desirable River Liffey view.\n\nThis apartment comprises of an entrance hallway, open plan living / dining area, kitchen, 2x double bedrooms and a bathroom. The apartment has an assigned carparking space in the development.\nOn entering the apartment we are greeted with a crisp white décor and light colour wood flooring, which continues through the apartment, giving a flow and continuity between the spaces.\nThe open plan living / dining area of the apartment is to the front with a beautiful River Liffey view looking out towards Smithfield. \nThe combination of the light colour décor and wood laminate flooring, along with the large windows, make this space feel bright and airy. \n\nThe kitchen is located off the living area, it has a combination of integrated and freestanding appliances. Fitted cabinets provide plenty of storage space, a white subway wall tile wrapping around the space is both stylish and practical, while the wooden countertop matches with the flooring.\n\nThe spacious double bedroom is to the rear of the apartment looking out on the private courtyard of the development. Great size wardrobes are fitted along the side to maximise floor space and there is ample space for additional bedroom furniture or a study / work-from-home station, if required. \n2nd bedroom is another great size bedroom, and could suit a variety of uses, including a home office or guest bedroom. A balcony is located off this room, and is looking out onto the courtyard of the development and has a desirable south-facing orientation.\n\nThe bathroom is fully tiled and has modern suite and shower fitted over the bath.\n\nAn always welcome additional storage space is located off the hallway. \n\nThe flooring throughout the apartment is a wood laminate, creating a nice flow and continuity through the rooms, with practical tile floor in the bathroom. \n\nThe heating throughout the apartment is updated electric and all windows are aluminium double glazed. \n\nThe development has fob / code access security doors and gates, all with intercoms throughout the entrance, common areas.\nOne carparking space is assigned to this apartment.\n\nManagement Company Fee: 2,372 / Annum (2026) \n\nFLOOR AREAS \nLIVING / DINING AREA 4.59m x 4.06m\nKITCHEN 1.71m x 2.21m \nPRIMARY BEDROOM 3.01m x 2.52m \nBEDROOM TWO 4.34m x 2.21m\nBATHROOM 1.78m x 2.22m \n+ STORAGE ROOM\n\nTOTAL FLOOR AREA 51.50m2 (554 sq ft) \n\n\nLOCATION \nThis Apartment is in the mature residential development of Pier 10, on Bridgefoot St, Dublin 8, in very close proximity to both desirable areas of Smithfield and the Liberties..\n The location boasts the ideal combination of being a quite mature residential development setting in a bustling City location, with excellent connectivity to the city centre. \nThe surrounding Smithfield & Stoneybatter area, just across the river regularly top lists for its desirability and has most recently featured in TimeOut Magazines Top 50 coolest neighbours in the world list. Smithfield Square just a 2min stroll from Pier 19 and is home to the Lighthouse Cinema and an array of bars, restaurants, and cafes. \nA further 5min walk north is Stoneybatter, which has a wide range of independent shops, bars, and restaurants (Mulligans, Grano, Joli Coffee and Wine, Slice, Lilliput Stores). \nIn the opposite direction, a 5min walk up Bridgefoot St to Thomas St brings you to the heart of the Liberties area of Dublin 8, an exciting south city location offering an array of excellent food, social and entertainment options on your door step while being only a short stroll to the City Centre, St. Stephens Green / Grafton St / Camden St areas. Local favourites such as Lucky`s, Spitalfields, and Fumbally Café, are all in close proximity, as well as a range of bars, cafes and restaurants that have recently opened in the surrounding area.\nA selection of supermarkets (Fresh, Tesco & Lidl) are all in close proximity. \nThe recently redesigned and landscaped Bridgefoot St Park is just around the corner and down the quay from the apartment is the beautiful historic Croppy Acres Park, in addition to the numerous small parks dotted around the area. The Phoenix Park is just 10min walk to the Parkgate St Entrance, with the Peoples Gardens, Dublin Zoo, and the Polo Grounds all an easy walk from the property. \nThe LUAS Smithfield Stop (Red Line) is just 200m from Pier 19, providing excellent access to the City Centre, Docklands / IFSC and Connolly Train Station. A number of Dublin Bus Routes service the area, Heuston Train Station is just one LUAS stop away. Cycling in and out of the city centre is popular with residents of the area, with a number of new bike lanes recently introduced. \n\n\nVIEWING IS HIGHLY RECOMMENDED & VIA CITYWIDE\n\n(These particulars do not constitute an offer or contract, and whilst every effort has been made in preparing all descriptions, dimensions, maps, and plans, these details should not be relied upon as fact. Dimensions / Illustrations are for guideline purposes only and not to scale. CITYWIDE will not hold itself responsible for any inaccuracies contained therein.)\n"
      },
